WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.165
Sir Richard's life improved, thanks to Robin Hood's gold.

2
00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:12.490
Crops filled his land and his castle was repaired and rebuilt.

3
00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:16.079
Robin had said his five hundred pounds was a gift.

4
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.047
But Sir Richard was determined to pay him back.

5
00:00:20.048 --> 00:00:24.963
One fine morning a year later, Sir Richard set out to return the money.

6
00:00:24.964 --> 00:00:28.397
He traveled with some of his own armed men.

7
00:00:28.398 --> 00:00:31.641
Three horses carried heavy packs and boxes.

8
00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:33.953
The men marched to the top of a hill.

9
00:00:33.954 --> 00:00:40.069
In the town below, they saw colorful flags and streamers waving in the breeze.

10
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.502
"What's happening in that town today?" asked Sir Richard.

11
00:00:43.503 --> 00:00:46.379
"A fair," replied one of his men.

12
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.427
"Many people go just to watch the wrestling matches.

13
00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:52.341
I heard there's a great prize for the winner."

14
00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:56.740
"That sounds interesting," said the knight. "Let's join them."

15
00:00:56.741 --> 00:00:59.617
The fair was held in the center of the town.

16
00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:04.102
On a green lawn, musicians were playing bagpipes.

17
00:01:04.103 --> 00:01:08.039
In a tent some people were dancing.

18
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.718
But the biggest crowd was gathered around the wrestling ring.

19
00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:14.704
Sir Richard and his men headed that way.

20
00:01:14.705 --> 00:01:17.684
A wrestling judge recognized the knight.

21
00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:22.462
"That's Sir Richard!" said the judge. "He's a good knight."

22
00:01:22.463 --> 00:01:27.423
"Let's invite him to sit with us," said the chief judge.

23
00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:31.618
So Sir Richard was soon sitting on the judges' platform.

24
00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:34.902
The chief judge pointed to a man in the ring.

25
00:01:34.903 --> 00:01:39.125
"Egbert from Stoke is the best wrestler today."

26
00:01:39.126 --> 00:01:42.593
"Who's wrestling against him?" asked Sir Richard.

27
00:01:42.594 --> 00:01:48.339
"One of our own men from this town," the chief judge said proudly.

28
00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.376
"He's known as William with the Scar."

29
00:01:53.377 --> 00:02:01.075
Sir Richard watched the wrestling match with great interest.

30
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:04.898
William with the Scar soon won the match.

31
00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:07.128
The crowd cheered.

32
00:02:07.136 --> 00:02:12.221
William walked all around the ring, daring anyone to wrestle him.

33
00:02:12.222 --> 00:02:16.859
"Who'd like to face me now?" he called to the crowd.

34
00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.935
"I'm the bravest wrestler in all the land!"

35
00:02:20.936 --> 00:02:25.247
Suddenly a loud voice cried out. "I'd like a turn!"

36
00:02:25.248 --> 00:02:27.732
A young man stepped into the ring.

37
00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:33.855
He was not as heavy as William, but he was taller and broader in the shoulders.

38
00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:36.580
The two men began to wrestle.

39
00:02:36.581 --> 00:02:39.839
It was clear they were almost equal in strength.

40
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:45.463
But suddenly the stranger grabbed William and threw him to the ground.

41
00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.298
William didn't get up.

42
00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:49.968
He lay there with his eyes closed.

43
00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:55.162
"If you've killed him, you're in trouble!" shouted one of the judges.

44
00:02:55.163 --> 00:02:57.736
"He's my cousin."

45
00:02:57.737 --> 00:03:02.251
"He knew the risks when he started to wrestle," said the stranger boldly.

46
00:03:02.252 --> 00:03:04.784
Richard turned to one of the judges.

47
00:03:04.785 --> 00:03:07.330
"He is right—the match was fair."

48
00:03:07.331 --> 00:03:11.015
Three men raced forward to lift William from the ground.

49
00:03:11.016 --> 00:03:17.204
Fortunately he was not dead, just dazed from his fall.

50
00:03:17.205 --> 00:03:20.715
The chief judge presented the prize to the stranger.

51
00:03:20.716 --> 00:03:25.470
"Young man, the prize is yours."

52
00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:29.327
The crowd booed.

53
00:03:29.328 --> 00:03:34.584
Sir Richard scratched his head as he stared at the winner, trying to recall his name.

54
00:03:34.585 --> 00:03:39.369
The stranger had beaten William so quickly and easily.

55
00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:44.109
Soon the young man left the ring and began to walk around the fair.

56
00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.283
People stared at the tall boy with the light hair and red cheeks.

57
00:03:48.284 --> 00:03:51.236
"Look at him!" said a woman.

58
00:03:51.237 --> 00:03:54.149
"He's showing off because he won."

59
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.327
"You only won because you cheated!" shouted a man.

60
00:03:58.328 --> 00:04:02.945
The stranger ignored the insults and went to watch the dancing.

61
00:04:02.946 --> 00:04:06.593
Suddenly a man threw a rock and hit him in the head.

62
00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:11.927
A burly blacksmith picked up a staff and shook it in a threatening way.

63
00:04:11.928 --> 00:04:14.632
More rocks were thrown at the stranger.

64
00:04:14.633 --> 00:04:18.320
Blood dripped from a cut on his forehead.

65
00:04:18.321 --> 00:04:24.417
Meanwhile Sir Richard had just remembered the young man's name and hurried after him.

66
00:04:24.418 --> 00:04:27.868
"Stop attacking him!" cried Sir Richard.

67
00:04:27.869 --> 00:04:30.882
"This is the great David of Doncaster.

68
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:35.416
David is one of the best wrestlers in England and one of Robin Hood's men!"

69
00:04:35.417 --> 00:04:41.221
The crowd gasped and stepped aside to let Sir Richard reach David.

70
00:04:41.222 --> 00:04:46.086
"Thanks for rescuing me," said David. "Robin will be grateful too."

71
00:04:46.087 --> 00:04:56.317
"I'm on my way to see Robin now," said Sir Richard. "Come with me."

72
00:04:56.318 --> 00:05:02.175
Robin Hood was waiting for Sir Richard when both men arrived in Sherwood Forest.

73
00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:05.480
Sir Richard leaped from his horse and hugged Robin.

74
00:05:05.481 --> 00:05:09.222
"I have kept my word and brought back the money you gave me."

75
00:05:09.223 --> 00:05:14.482
At first Robin refused to take Sir Richard's money, but the knight insisted.

76
00:05:14.483 --> 00:05:18.370
"Put this money in our treasury," said Robin to David.

77
00:05:18.371 --> 00:05:21.542
"We used our five hundred pounds to help Sir Richard.

78
00:05:21.543 --> 00:05:26.758
Now we'll use his gold to help someone else!"

